    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/5/65179.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "Hello friends and welcome to another episode of the Jenna Ellis Show. I'm Jenna Ellis and we are on House Speaker Watch. So today has been no different than yesterday in terms of all of the drama that is unfolding on the congressional floor. And some people think this is great because this finally means that we're seeing the debate. We're seeing the back and forth. Other people think, you know, hey, these 20 at least that are opposing Kevin McCarthy really need to be team players and the infighting isn't good. So I think overall, regardless of what side you fall on, this discussion is a very, very good thing, not just for the party, but also for the country. But joining me now is my good friend Doug Collins, who is the host of the Doug Collins podcast right here on Salem Podcast Network and a former member of Congress from the great state of Georgia. So Doug, You would know this better than me, and as we were discussing right before the show, you know, you have lived through the past eight years of kind of this percolating. So what are your thoughts going into now what is likely going to end up being, you know, potentially double digits of votes and losses for Kevin McCarthy? Where do we go from here?",
