    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "I love that show. And look, it had a liberal band, but it had a lot of conservative, but if you remember that time when they went into the, it was the Santo selection, it was the, you know, the Alan Alda, the characters, They came to a time that they said, you know, one vote, you know, one four vote, five, two votes, three votes, it's ridiculous. And we're getting to that point now. And this is, I said this before earlier today on this vote. That the pressure is no longer on the 20 who have voted against Kevin McCarthy. The pressure is on Kevin McCarthy. The 20 who've already made their choice and made their determination. There's no going back on that, especially if they don't get anything quote for what they're doing. Um, they're in no pressure at all now. It's Kevin McCarthy who's under pressure now to either say, look, I gave it my best shot and my lifelong dream is now over. And after spending the last six years on my road, electing many of the same ones who are now opposing me. Um, I just, I'll drop off, I'll nominate somebody else, and then I'm going to walk off the world stage, which is probably what would happen. But let's take a step back. This didn't happen this month. This didn't happen this year. This has been started all the way back in 2010 and 11 really when the first group of new conservatives came in after the Tea Party issue of the Obamacare, Dodd-Frank, and this was under, remember the leadership at back then, of Boehner, Canner, McCarthy, and Ryan, who brought in this new group, not sure how to deal with it. Every year since then, Republicans had struggles, at least minor struggles, most behind the scenes, on electing the speaker. It became a badge of honor for some to not vote for Ryan, or Boehner, or anybody else for that matter. And all it did was sort of mask what was going on underneath. And this is now full blown because the, the 20 had the ability to, but think about this, Jenna, if, if the, Republicans had done what we had hoped they would have done in the House and got a 25-30 seat majority we wouldn't be having this conversation.",
