  {
    "episode_id": 65179,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/5/65179.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "That's a great point that it's only because of the slight Republican majority and the lack of this overwhelming red wave that you even have the possibility of this type of debate on the House floor and maybe ultimately this will be a good thing maybe this has been percolating for the last over a decade and, you know, you're seeing a lot of people on social media, you know, whether or not Twitter is really a temperature of the average American, I don't know, but there are a lot of people that are in these polls and are tweeting and not just people who are in politics, you know, like you and I are in terms of the nitty gritty every day, but, you know, some just regular Americans who are sick and tired of the establishment They're tired of whether it's just establishment versus Democrat. And so they want this type of pushback. They want this type of change. So in your mind, is that type of change really what's behind the people like Chip Roy and Matt Gates? Is this just a self-serving type of posturing or are they really trying to accomplish something that now just because of the lack of red wave, they're finally getting the opportunity to do that?",
