  {
    "episode_id": 65179,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/5/65179.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "I look at the end. I don't want a certain motive here. Okay. And I'm not going to to Matt, who's a good friend. I know Chip very well. I mean, these, these, I got friends on both sides of this. I worked out with well, all of them. But let me just say it a few things. Number one, they wouldn't be doing this if they had a, if there was a 20 post late, they may vote 20 against Kevin McCarthy, but it wouldn't matter. Kevin would have the more votes and it'd be over with this would be done. Um, I think part of this goes back to the summer when Kevin thought that he was going to have more votes to play with so he didn't engage the negotiations earlier. So again, it's a little bit coming back to bite it. But at the end of the day, this is frankly, this has become personal. I mean, I heard it in the last speech that was given. by Lauren Bober. I was called by the former president and told not to do this. Well, maybe he should call Kevin. And you also heard it in Warren Davidson speech. I know Warren who nominated Kevin for this fifth ballot that is just happening in this day. And it was interesting to hear him say some things. And I sat back and watched some of these same individuals and the same conversations flip the circuit here. I mean, back when we were trying to get tax reform done, health care done. It was like, you know, you know, there was no talk of this team player stuff. It was not get to 2018. It was like, well, you got to add my amendment or I'm not going to vote for it. And so it's sort of come full circle here. And I'm not throwing off on anybody, but you can't always play the antagonist and get what you want. And then quote Reagan saying, you're going to get every, you know, you'll, you'll try to compromise and get what's, you know, as best you can. I've always been an 80% person. You know, if I can get 80% of what I'm looking for... I'm going to go with it because I can always come back and get more. 80% is better than zero. And this has become the whole process. I've talked to members in the last few hours and days that are just, I'm not sure where they go back in this. Let's just say even Kevin gets by and they get another speaker, put in your whoever name is, they're going to have a hard time. But the relational fraction that you're seeing right now is very concerning, should be for conservatives. Uh, especially to try and get anything done. I mean, if they can't do this on speaker, where are they going to get on debt ceiling? Where are they going to get on appropriations bills? Where are they going to get on immigration? And look, I'm tired of this idea that you can only get what all you want. You got to put the best conservative foot forward. That's what's got to happen. And right now we're not doing that. And, you know, so as you look at this long term, Um, there is self service on both sides. I mean, let's just face it. But at a certain point in time, also, we've, I think you made a point about Twitter. I believe Twitter is a good representation of Twitter. I don't believe it's a good representation of much anything else. If that be true, then Republicans would have dominated in every, you know, race, especially conservative Twitter. Um, it wouldn't, it just didn't happen. But I do what thing you made a mention about people are tired. What people are tired of Jen is being lied to. What people are being tired to say, and I'll go back to something and I've said this before and it irritates some of my conservative friends. And I frankly, I'm over it. I don't care. Okay. We lied to the American people and the group that got elected in 10 and got elected no time. They lied to the American people saying we will overthrow Obamacare. We will do away with Obamacare. That's a lie. There was no way they could. I mean, you're a lawyer. There's just only so many things. I mean, they didn't have the Senate. They didn't have the presidency who actually his name was on the legislation. But yet we went out and heard it over and over again, elect us, and we will overthrow Obamacare. They're not and guess what Obamacare is still around today. I mean we were able to make huge chunks and here's what saddens me. We got eight or nine things that basically gutted Obamacare is it took from many ways but yet we never could talk about it because only thing that many people said well you said you were gonna get rid of it. I said well no I did I said I'm gonna kill try to kill it the best way I can. But this is what happens. So we've got to get his Republicans a better messaging to say, OK, here's what we're going to try and do. Here's what we're going to push forward and we're going to continue. You give us more votes. We can fix it. Give us a Senate. We can fix it. But you got to move forward and we've not been moving forward.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
