  {
    "episode_id": 65179,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/5/65179.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, that is such a great point. And I think that even some of the promises that have been made by the new majority are a little bit inflated in terms of what can actually be done. I mean, there's talk about, you know, having some of these 87,000 IRS agents and scaling that back. But I mean, it's something like that. There's no possible pathway to that. if we don't control the Senate and we don't have a veto-proof majority in order to accomplish that type of legislation. So when we're looking at the leadership of the speaker, at least for the next two years until 2024, what realistically are you looking for from the conservative Republican majority? And does the office of the speaker actually matter in terms of accomplishing that?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
