    "turn_text": "And so this is where this diversity among the bays, we aren't unified because we don't all think exactly alike, and we should all start with some fundamental principles, of course, but we need to realize that this is a legislative body, It's not a bunch of kings that are all getting together and they each have dominion over their district in terms of tyranny. This isn't what this is. And so looking at what the accomplishments of a Congress can genuinely be under a constitutional framework. the intention and purpose of the legislature and then what we can actually do, that makes a lot more sense than just shouting to the wind of saying, you know, we're never getting anything done because we didn't get 100% and look at how far the Democrats are taking this country down the drain.",
