    "turn_text": "The sad part is there's no deadline. This is just, I mean, history has gone as long as six months. I will tell you this. If this goes on longer, let's just say I'm only use a wild example. If we get into the weekend and we don't have a speaker, I'm fearful for the Republican brand and majority going forward. You're going to lose people, folks. This is a concerning part. I figure this will end by the next 24 to 48 hours. But don't underestimate how hard this is, I think, for Kevin McCarthy. Everybody says, well, you just ought to give up. You've put everything in your life. We may disagree on a lot of things. Kevin, you look at the voting record. I mean, you stuck by Donald Trump. I mean, think about the things here. And you're asking him, basically, to give up. I mean, he spent like 200 and something nights this year on the road, supporting candidates and raising money to get this four-seat majority. Here's the thing I remind people all the time. If you don't have those, quote, moderates from New York and other states, and what we have now is Biden districts, you know what you have? You have a minority of, quote, hardcore conservatives that are a hundred and something seat minority and never have a hope of doing anything.",
